\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {V}{\ignorespaces Angular power spectrum of the chirality asymmetry map (Catalog~C, equivariant). The first row is the canonical \emph  {single-mode} $\ell \!=\!1$ post-MASTER result that anchors the dipole-isotropy null (companion artifact \artifact  {pipelines/p2\_chirality/master\_results/master\_power\_spectrum.json}, $\ell _1$\,dipole entry; analysis subsample $n\!=\!5{,}547{,}858$, $f_{\rm  sky}\!=\!0.659$). Rows 2--5 are five-mode \emph  {bandpowers} $\ell \!\in \![\ell _{\rm  eff}\!-\!2,\,\ell _{\rm  eff}\!+\!2]$ from the canonical-$N$ MASTER recompute on the full $N_{\rm  spiral}\!=\!3{,}201{,}160$ / $f_{\rm  sky}\!=\!0.491$ analysis (companion artifact \artifact  {pipelines/p2\_chirality/r42\_results/wave\_14\_pp\_namaster\_verification.json}; $500$ MC realizations for the post-MASTER $\ell \!=\!1$ single-mode row only; the $\ell \!\geq \!2$ bandpower rows use the cheaper $N_{\rm  MC}\!=\!1{,}000$ bootstrap-of-CW-labels null without mode-coupling inversion). $\sigma _{\rm  null}$ is the per-bin standard deviation of the MC null distribution at that bandpower. Higher-bandpower $\sim \!2\sigma $ values reflect residual coupling of the $9.5\sigma $ monopole into low-$\ell $ bandpowers under the partial-sky MASTER kernel; the isotropy-breaking dipole observable is the single-mode $\ell \!=\!1$ result (first row), and the bandpower table is a null-consistency cross-check at multipoles \emph  {other than} the dipole. The canonical-$N$ MASTER direct-MC at $\ell \!=\!1$ on the equivariant map (direct single-mode NaMaster MC at canonical $f_{\rm  sky}$) yields $\sigma _{\rm  canonical}\!=\!+3.64$ at $f_{\rm  sky}\!=\!0.49005$, $N_{\rm  spiral}\!=\!3{,}201{,}160$, SEED$\,=\,42$, $500$-MC (Sec.~\ref {sec:conclusions} and companion artifact \artifact  {pipelines/p2\_chirality/outputs/canonical\_provenance/canonical\_n\_master\_l1\_direct.json}); this is a sub-detection-threshold canonical-mask excess reported transparently as an unresolved systematic pending matched-pipeline reanalysis, not a calibrated leakage floor calibration, with the $-0.122\sigma $ subsample-mask figure retained as the headline post-MASTER null because its $f_{\rm  sky}\!=\!0.659$ mask is a strict superset that bypasses the canonical-mask leakage channel.}}{18}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:multipole}{{V}{18}{Angular power spectrum of the chirality asymmetry map (Catalog~C, equivariant). The first row is the canonical \emph {single-mode} $\ell \!=\!1$ post-MASTER result that anchors the dipole-isotropy null (companion artifact \artifact {pipelines/p2\_chirality/master\_results/master\_power\_spectrum.json}, $\ell _1$\,dipole entry; analysis subsample $n\!=\!5{,}547{,}858$, $f_{\rm sky}\!=\!0.659$). Rows 2--5 are five-mode \emph {bandpowers} $\ell \!\in \![\ell _{\rm eff}\!-\!2,\,\ell _{\rm eff}\!+\!2]$ from the canonical-$N$ MASTER recompute on the full $N_{\rm spiral}\!=\!3{,}201{,}160$ / $f_{\rm sky}\!=\!0.491$ analysis (companion artifact \artifact {pipelines/p2\_chirality/r42\_results/wave\_14\_pp\_namaster\_verification.json}; $500$ MC realizations for the post-MASTER $\ell \!=\!1$ single-mode row only; the $\ell \!\geq \!2$ bandpower rows use the cheaper $N_{\rm MC}\!=\!1{,}000$ bootstrap-of-CW-labels null without mode-coupling inversion). $\sigma _{\rm null}$ is the per-bin standard deviation of the MC null distribution at that bandpower. Higher-bandpower $\sim \!2\sigmaunit $ values reflect residual coupling of the $9.5\sigmaunit $ monopole into low-$\ell $ bandpowers under the partial-sky MASTER kernel; the isotropy-breaking dipole observable is the single-mode $\ell \!=\!1$ result (first row), and the bandpower table is a null-consistency cross-check at multipoles \emph {other than} the dipole. The canonical-$N$ MASTER direct-MC at $\ell \!=\!1$ on the equivariant map (direct single-mode NaMaster MC at canonical $f_{\rm sky}$) yields $\sigma _{\rm canonical}\!=\!+3.64$ at $f_{\rm sky}\!=\!0.49005$, $N_{\rm spiral}\!=\!3{,}201{,}160$, SEED$\,=\,42$, $500$-MC (Sec.~\ref {sec:conclusions} and companion artifact \artifact {pipelines/p2\_chirality/outputs/canonical\_provenance/canonical\_n\_master\_l1\_direct.json}); this is a sub-detection-threshold canonical-mask excess reported transparently as an unresolved systematic pending matched-pipeline reanalysis, not a calibrated leakage floor calibration, with the $-0.122\sigmaunit $ subsample-mask figure retained as the headline post-MASTER null because its $f_{\rm sky}\!=\!0.659$ mask is a strict superset that bypasses the canonical-mask leakage channel}{table.5}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {D}Monopole+Mask Leakage Generative Null}{20}{section*.27}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:monopole_mask_null}{{IV\,D}{20}{}{section*.27}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Angular power spectrum of the chirality asymmetry map (Catalog~C, equivariant) for multipoles $\ell = 1$--$5$. Black points show the measured $C_\ell $ values; the gray band indicates the $1\sigma $ and $2\sigma $ envelopes from 1{,}000 Monte Carlo null realizations at the canonical $N_{\rm  spiral}=3{,}201{,}160$ shot-noise normalization. The MASTER-deconvolved $\ell =1$ value is $-0.12\sigma $ on the analysis subsample mask (the headline null; see Sec.~\ref {sec:dipole}); the canonical-$N$ direct-MC result $+3.64\sigma $ (Sec.~\ref {sec:conclusions}, $f_{\rm  sky}=0.49005$, $N_{\rm  spiral}=3{,}201{,}160$) is a mild canonical-mask excess resolved by the v1.0.108 multi-null battery: the proper-monopole-subtracted binomial null gives $+3.64\sigma $ (data $C_1$ correctly subtracted), the apodized canonical mask gives $+3.57\sigma $ (ruling out sharp-edge NaMaster artifacts), and a direct cross-spectrum with pixel-density gives $\sigma _{\ell =1}\!=\!-1.53$ with $r_{\ell =1}\!=\!-0.49$ at the auto-spectrum dipole multipole AND $\sigma _{\ell =2}\!=\!-2.89$ at quadrupole anti-alignment with $r_{\ell =2}\!=\!-0.65$ (depth-correlated systematic at BOTH $\ell \!=\!1$ AND $\ell \!=\!2$ DIRECTLY CONFIRMED --- R20-Grok-B2 closure: the $\ell \!=\!1$ cross-spectrum is now reported as the per-Grok-R20 request; both multipoles show negative correlation with the pixel-density proxy, with $\ell \!=\!2$ at higher significance). The bootstrap pixel-resample test gives $-0.22\sigma $ for the data but is TAUTOLOGICAL for cosmological-dipole hypothesis testing per the v1.0.110-v1.0.111 injection-recovery audit (a REAL injected $A\!=\!1.7\%$ dipole also gives median $\sigma \!=\!-0.49$ under the same bootstrap) and is therefore reported only as a sampling-variance diagnostic, not as a verdict. The three discriminators that rigorously rule out interpretation~(i) "real cosmological dipole at $\sim \!1.7\%$" are: (a)~$\ell \!=\!2 > \ell \!=\!1$ broadband structure (incompatible with a clean dipole), (b)~$p_{\rm  eq}$ quality-quartile washout (all four quartiles $|\sigma |<1$), and (c)~direct cross-spectrum quadrupole anti-alignment with the pixel-density proxy. Under this three-discriminator framework not assigned a physical interpretation in this manuscript. Several low-$\ell $ bandpowers are formally above null at $+2$ to $+6\sigma $ in the pre-deconvolution pseudo-$C_\ell $ and are attributed to the same monopole--mask leakage channel; they are not interpreted as parity dipoles. Verification artifact: \artifact  {pipelines/h200\_results/wave11c\_nspiral\_recompute\_2026-05-01/results.json}. The no-dipole-at-$\ell =1$ verdict at the catalog's empirical $\geq 0.75\%$ empirical $50\%$-recovery-$3\sigma $ threshold (Sec.~\ref {sec:sensitivity}) is carried by the full-catalog $0.43\sigma $ real-space dipole and the strict-superset $-0.12\sigma $ MASTER result which both bypass the canonical-mask leakage channel. The spatially uniform monopole offset (across all 7 equatorial coordinate slabs) is $0.26\%$ (see Sec.~\ref {sec:cw_frac}). }}{20}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:multipoles}{{8}{20}{Angular power spectrum of the chirality asymmetry map (Catalog~C, equivariant) for multipoles $\ell = 1$--$5$. Black points show the measured $C_\ell $ values; the gray band indicates the $1\sigmaunit $ and $2\sigmaunit $ envelopes from 1{,}000 Monte Carlo null realizations at the canonical $N_{\rm spiral}=3{,}201{,}160$ shot-noise normalization. The MASTER-deconvolved $\ell =1$ value is $-0.12\sigmaunit $ on the analysis subsample mask (the headline null; see Sec.~\ref {sec:dipole}); the canonical-$N$ direct-MC result $+3.64\sigmaunit $ (Sec.~\ref {sec:conclusions}, $f_{\rm sky}=0.49005$, $N_{\rm spiral}=3{,}201{,}160$) is a mild canonical-mask excess resolved by the v1.0.108 multi-null battery: the proper-monopole-subtracted binomial null gives $+3.64\sigmaunit $ (data $C_1$ correctly subtracted), the apodized canonical mask gives $+3.57\sigmaunit $ (ruling out sharp-edge NaMaster artifacts), and a direct cross-spectrum with pixel-density gives $\sigma _{\ell =1}\!=\!-1.53$ with $r_{\ell =1}\!=\!-0.49$ at the auto-spectrum dipole multipole AND $\sigma _{\ell =2}\!=\!-2.89$ at quadrupole anti-alignment with $r_{\ell =2}\!=\!-0.65$ (depth-correlated systematic at BOTH $\ell \!=\!1$ AND $\ell \!=\!2$ DIRECTLY CONFIRMED --- R20-Grok-B2 closure: the $\ell \!=\!1$ cross-spectrum is now reported as the per-Grok-R20 request; both multipoles show negative correlation with the pixel-density proxy, with $\ell \!=\!2$ at higher significance). The bootstrap pixel-resample test gives $-0.22\sigmaunit $ for the data but is TAUTOLOGICAL for cosmological-dipole hypothesis testing per the v1.0.110-v1.0.111 injection-recovery audit (a REAL injected $A\!=\!1.7\%$ dipole also gives median $\sigma \!=\!-0.49$ under the same bootstrap) and is therefore reported only as a sampling-variance diagnostic, not as a verdict. The three discriminators that rigorously rule out interpretation~(i) "real cosmological dipole at $\sim \!1.7\%$" are: (a)~$\ell \!=\!2 > \ell \!=\!1$ broadband structure (incompatible with a clean dipole), (b)~$p_{\rm eq}$ quality-quartile washout (all four quartiles $|\sigma |<1$), and (c)~direct cross-spectrum quadrupole anti-alignment with the pixel-density proxy. Under this three-discriminator framework not assigned a physical interpretation in this manuscript. Several low-$\ell $ bandpowers are formally above null at $+2$ to $+6\sigmaunit $ in the pre-deconvolution pseudo-$C_\ell $ and are attributed to the same monopole--mask leakage channel; they are not interpreted as parity dipoles. Verification artifact: \artifact {pipelines/h200\_results/wave11c\_nspiral\_recompute\_2026-05-01/results.json}. The no-dipole-at-$\ell =1$ verdict at the catalog's empirical $\geq 0.75\%$ empirical $50\%$-recovery-$3\sigma $ threshold (Sec.~\ref {sec:sensitivity}) is carried by the full-catalog $0.43\sigmaunit $ real-space dipole and the strict-superset $-0.12\sigmaunit $ MASTER result which both bypass the canonical-mask leakage channel. The spatially uniform monopole offset (across all 7 equatorial coordinate slabs) is $0.26\%$ (see Sec.~\ref {sec:cw_frac})}{figure.8}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {VI}{\ignorespaces Monopole+mask leakage null (canonical mask, NSIDE$\,=\,$64, $f_{\rm  sky}\!=\!0.49005$ (canonical, from \artifact  {pipelines/p2\_chirality/outputs/canonical\_provenance/monopole\_mask\_null\_results.json}: $n_{\rm  spiral,in\,mask}\!=\!3{,}200{,}420$ of $n_{\rm  spiral,total}\!=\!3{,}201{,}160$; $24{,}087$ NSIDE$=64$ pixels with $\geq \!10$ spirals), seed$\,=\,$42; $N\!=\!500$ binomial-monopole realizations of $p_{\rm  CW}^{\rm  global}\!=\!0.4974$ on the canonical spiral-count map). Pre-MASTER pseudo-$C_\ell ^{(\ell =1)}$ and hemisphere max$|A|$ reported with their data $z$-score against the null (the post-MASTER decoupled $C_\ell $ at $\ell \!=\!1$ is reported in Sec.~\ref {sec:dipole} under a different null model and is not included in this table; see Table~\ref {tab:headline_summary} footnote b). The N=500 simulation supersedes the v1.0.69 smoke result at N=25; the monopole-only null reproduces $99.3\%$ of the observed (computed as the ratio $1.6846\!\times \!10^{-2}\!/1.696\!\times \!10^{-2}\!=\!0.9932$ from Table~\ref {tab:monopole_mask_null}) pre-MASTER pseudo-$C_\ell ^{(\ell =1)}$ power (residual $+1.68\sigma $) and $48.6\%$ of the hemisphere max-amplitude (residual $+4.42\sigma $). Verification: \artifact  {pipelines/p2\_chirality/outputs/canonical\_provenance/monopole\_mask\_null\_results.json}. }}{21}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:monopole_mask_null}{{VI}{21}{Monopole+mask leakage null (canonical mask, NSIDE$\,=\,$64, $f_{\rm sky}\!=\!0.49005$ (canonical, from \artifact {pipelines/p2\_chirality/outputs/canonical\_provenance/monopole\_mask\_null\_results.json}: $n_{\rm spiral,in\,mask}\!=\!3{,}200{,}420$ of $n_{\rm spiral,total}\!=\!3{,}201{,}160$; $24{,}087$ NSIDE$=64$ pixels with $\geq \!10$ spirals), seed$\,=\,$42; $N\!=\!500$ binomial-monopole realizations of $p_{\rm CW}^{\rm global}\!=\!0.4974$ on the canonical spiral-count map). Pre-MASTER pseudo-$C_\ell ^{(\ell =1)}$ and hemisphere max$|A|$ reported with their data $z$-score against the null (the post-MASTER decoupled $C_\ell $ at $\ell \!=\!1$ is reported in Sec.~\ref {sec:dipole} under a different null model and is not included in this table; see Table~\ref {tab:headline_summary} footnote b). The N=500 simulation supersedes the v1.0.69 smoke result at N=25; the monopole-only null reproduces $99.3\%$ of the observed (computed as the ratio $1.6846\!\times \!10^{-2}\!/1.696\!\times \!10^{-2}\!=\!0.9932$ from Table~\ref {tab:monopole_mask_null}) pre-MASTER pseudo-$C_\ell ^{(\ell =1)}$ power (residual $+1.68\sigmaunit $) and $48.6\%$ of the hemisphere max-amplitude (residual $+4.42\sigmaunit $). Verification: \artifact {pipelines/p2\_chirality/outputs/canonical\_provenance/monopole\_mask\_null\_results.json}}{table.6}{}}
